# Harness-home env file, read by dsh at startup.
#
# Only credential-style names may live here. dsh refuses to start when this
# file sets a bootstrap variable, because those decide how the process starts
# or how it reaches the network and only the launching environment may supply
# them. That list is BOOTSTRAP_NAMES plus the DSH_ / XDG_ / DYLD_ / BASH_FUNC_
# prefixes in @deepseek-ai/dsh-app-boot, and it includes the DeepSeek base-URL
# variable. Setting the base URL here once made `dsh web` abort with "only the
# launching environment may set" before it ever listened, which the app then
# reported as a 240-second startup timeout.
#
# So the app exports the base URL itself -- it points the guest at the
# host-side forwarder on 127.0.0.1:31337, since iOS will not let the guest's
# own sockets leave the sandbox. The model credential is what belongs here: it
# is a supported read-only fallback, ranked below the managed
# $DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml store that the Models page writes.
#
# To sign in without opening the Models page, add one line below this comment
# holding the key variable name, an equals sign, and the key. Comments only,
# otherwise: a name dsh considers bootstrap-only will stop it from starting.
